(window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY = window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY || {})["2026-09-18"] = {"meta":{"id":"2026-09-18","label":"2026 年 9 月 18 日","date":"2026-09-18","range":"","theme":"商业","themes":["商业"],"sources":["Economist"],"title":"Silicon dunes","titleZh":"硅丘","counts":{"article":0,"paragraph":9,"vocab":28,"question":20,"qa":0,"original":5,"layout":1},"tabs":{"articles":false,"reading":true,"tests":true,"qa":false,"originals":true}},"articles":[],"reading":[{"file":"9.18 精读(1).pdf","headline":{"title":"Silicon dunes","titleZh":"硅丘","source":"Economist","series":"考研那些事儿之商业系列"},"paragraphs":[{"index":1,"en":"Soon after war broke out in the Gulf, Iranian drones targeted Amazon’s data centres in the United Arab Emirates (UAE) and Bahrain. But at Stargate UAE, a 1-gigawatt data centre being built on a 5GW campus in Abu Dhabi, work “never stopped,” says an executive at a state- backed artificial-intelligence firm. The first 200-megawatt phase is almost complete.","zh":"海湾地区战事爆发后不久，伊朗无人机便将亚马逊位于阿联酋(UAE)和巴林的数据中心列为打击目标。但在“星际之门阿联酋”（StargateUAE），据一位某国资人工智能公司的高管表示，建设工作“从未停止”。该在建项目位于阿布扎比一个5吉瓦园区内，落成后会是一座1吉瓦数据中心。目前首期200兆瓦阶段已接近完工。"},{"index":2,"en":"Last year PwC, a consultancy, predicted that across the Gulf data- centre capacity would rise fourfold within five years, to about 4GW. The outbreak of war has not halted the boom. HUMAIN, an AI company established by Saudi Arabia’s sovereign-wealth fund, announced last month that it would build a facility with DataVolt, another Saudi firm, at Oxagon, an industrial city on the country’s west coast. Two other Saudi outfits, Axelerated Solutions and Al Moammar Information Systems, have also trumpeted new data-centre investments.","zh":"去年，咨询机构普华永道预测，整个海湾地区的数据中心容量将在五年内扩大至四倍，达到约4吉瓦。战事爆发并未遏止这一热潮。由沙特主权财富基金设立的人工智能公司HUMAIN上月宣布，将与另一家沙特企业DataVolt合作，在沙特西海岸工业城市奥克萨贡共建一座数据中心。另外两家沙特公司"},{"index":3,"en":"America’s hyperscalers, too, seem to have lost none of their enthusiasm. In September Amazon Web Services said it was expanding a partnership with HUMAIN to provide more data-centre capacity by 2028. Last month Microsoft, which has leased Saudi sites from Al Moammar and is working with Du, an Emirati telecom firm, to build a data centre in the UAE, said it would bring more regional capacity online in November.","zh":"美国超大规模云厂商似乎同样热情不减。9月，亚马逊云服务表示，正在扩大与HUMAIN的合作，以期在2028年前提供更多数据中心容量。上月，微软表示将于11月启用更多区域容量；该公司已从AlMoammar租用沙特站点，并正与阿联酋电信企业Du合作，在阿联酋建设数据中心。"},{"index":4,"en":"Several factors explain the region’s continued attraction, despite the conflict. One is cheap energy: electricity tariffs in the Gulf are around six cents per kilowatt hour, compared with between nine and 15 cents in America, reports PwC. Vast amounts of renewable power and new transmission infrastructure have pushed costs lower. Another is cheap land: according to PwC, industrial land for data centres in Saudi Arabia costs $10-50 per square metre, well below the $150-600 in northern Virginia, where many of America’s server farms live. McKinsey, another consultancy, puts the cost of building and powering a 100-megawatt AI data centre in the Gulf at $200-220 per MW hour, nearly as low as in China.","zh":"尽管战争冲突持续，该地区仍具吸引力，原因有几点。其一是能源价格低廉：普华永道报告称，海湾地区电价约为每千瓦时6美分，而美国为9至15美分。大量可再生能源和新输电基础设施进一步压低了成本。其二是土地价格低廉：据普华永道数据，沙特数据中心工业用地价格为每平方米10至50美元，远低于美国北弗吉尼亚州的150至600美元，美国许多服务器集群便坐落于此。另一家咨询机构麦肯锡估算，在海湾地区建设和供电一座100兆瓦人工智能数据中心，成本为每兆瓦时200至220美元，低到几乎与中国相当。"},{"index":5,"en":"The Gulf has also established itself as a hub for industry talent: last year the UAE and Saudi Arabia were among the countries that recorded the highest net inflow of AI workers relative to their workforces. There is no evidence that war has sent this flow of talent into reverse.","zh":"海湾地区还确立了其行业人才中心的地位：去年，阿联酋和沙特阿拉伯的人工智能人才净流入量（相对于其劳动力规模而言）位于全球前列。而且，目前没有证据表明，战事已使这一人才流入趋势发生逆转。"},{"index":6,"en":"Then there are the Gulf states’deep pockets. In July MGX, an Emirati state-run fund, raised $50bn to invest in AI. Most of that money will flow to overseas companies, but those wanting a slice of it will be eager to keep their paymasters happy by investing in the region.","zh":"此外，海湾国家财力雄厚。7月，阿联酋国有基金MGX筹集500亿美元用于投资人工智能。其中大部分资金将流向海外企业，但希望从中分一杯羹的企业，将急于通过在该地区投资来让出资方满意。"},{"index":7,"en":"Domestic policies in the Gulf will require more data centres, in effect underwriting demand. In April the UAE said it would deploy “agentic AI” across half of the government. The country’s National Cloud Security Policy requires “operational sovereignty” for government entities and operators of critical infrastructure, further supporting the build-out, while Saudi Arabia’s financial institutions are generally required to use cloud services within the country. Luca Bennici of McKinsey notes that private firms in the Gulf have “growing concerns” of their own about data protection and sovereignty.","zh":"海湾国家的国内政策将需要更多数据中心，这实际上为需求提供了担保。4月，阿联酋表示将在半数政府部门部署“代理式人工智能”。该国《国家云安全政策》要求政府实体和关键基础设施运营者实现“运营主权”，这进一步支撑了数据中心扩建；沙特阿拉伯的金融机构则普遍被要求使用境内云服务。麦肯锡的卢卡·本尼奇（LucaBennici）指出，海湾地区私营企业对数据保护和主权问题“的担忧在日益加剧”。"},{"index":8,"en":"What is more, there is little of the public opposition to data centres increasingly on show in the West, where many people resent power- hungry facilities on their doorstep. Bashing data centres has turned into a popular campaign strategy in American politics. In the Gulf, not so much. “Centralised decision making” helps, says an executive in the region.","zh":"更重要的是，西方公众针对数据中心的反对日益显现，许多人对住所附近的高耗能设施感到不满，但这种情况在海湾地区却很少见。抨击数据中心已在美国政治成为一种流行的竞选策略。在海湾地区则不然。该地区一位高管表示，这得益于“集中决策”。"},{"index":9,"en":"True, the war has disrupted the Gulf’s carefully crafted economic boom. It has also made the region’s rulers more determined to make their digital investments secure. Kurt Davis junior of Alvarez & Marsal, one more consultancy, notes that plans to make data centres as safe as embassies, even putting them underground, are being mooted. Nevertheless, the build-out continues.","zh":"诚然，战争扰乱了海湾地区精心打造的经济繁荣。但战争也使该地区的执政者更加坚定地要保障其数字投资的安全。另一家咨询机构Alvarez&Marsal的小库尔特·戴维斯（KurtDavisjunior）指出，计划将数据中心打造得如使馆般安全、甚至将其设于地下的方案正在酝酿中。尽管如此，数据中心扩建仍在继续。"}],"vocab":[{"term":"dune","head":"n. /duːn/ a small hill of sand formed by the wind, near","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"theseaorinadesert（风吹积成的）沙丘","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"halt","head":"v. to stop; to make sb/sth stop（使）停止，停下【️【️考研","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"The trial was halted after the first week. 第一周结束后，审判 暂停。","tags":[]},{"term":"break out phrase if something such as war, fighting, or","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"disease breaks out, it begins suddenly (战争、殴斗、疾病等)","exampleZh":"爆发 He was 29 when war broke out. 战争爆发时他 29 岁。","tags":[]},{"term":"drone","head":"n. /drəʊn/ an aircraft without a pilot, controlled from","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"theground无人驾驶飞机","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"gigawattn./ˈɡɪɡəˌwɒt/吉瓦，千兆瓦，十亿瓦特","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"海湾地区战事爆发后不久，伊朗无人机便将亚马逊位于阿联","exampleZh":"酋(UAE)和巴林的数据中心列为打击目标。但在“星际之门阿联 酋”（StargateUAE），据一位某国资人工智能公司的高管表示， 建设工作“从未停止”。该在建项目位于阿布扎比一个5吉瓦园 区内，落成后会是一座1吉瓦数据中心。目前首期200兆瓦阶 段已接近完工。","tags":[]},{"term":"fourfold","head":"adv. /ˈfɔːfəʊld/ by or up to four times as many or","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"asmuch四倍地","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"sovereign-wealth fund","head":"n. / ˈ s ɒ vr ɪ n/ a state-owned","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"investmentfund主权财富基金(一种国家拥有的投资基金)","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"outfit","head":"n. /ˈaʊtfɪt/ a group of people working together as an","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"organization, business, team, etc.团队；小组；分队【️【️考研大","exampleZh":"纲词汇】 a market research outfit 市场调查组","tags":[]},{"term":"trumpet","head":"v. /ˈtrʌmpɪt/ ~ sth (as sth) to talk about sth","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"publicly in a proud or enthusiastic way 宣扬；鼓吹；吹嘘【️【️考","exampleZh":"研大纲词汇】 to trumpet sb's achievements 吹嘘某人的成就 去年，咨询机构普华永道预测，整个海湾地区的数据中心容 量将在五年内扩大至四倍，达到约4吉瓦。战事爆发并未遏止这 一热潮。由沙特主权财富基金设立的人工智能公司HUMAIN上 月宣布，将与另一家沙特企业DataVolt合作，在沙特西海岸工 业城市奥克萨贡共建一座数据中心。另外两家沙特公司 Axelerated Solutions和Al Moammar Information Systems， 也高调公布了新的数据中心投资。","tags":[]},{"term":"hyperscaler","head":"n. /ˈhaɪpərˌskeɪlər/ 超大规模云服务商：指拥有","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"极大规模的数据中心和基础设施，能够向客户提供海量算力、存","exampleZh":"储及云服务的顶尖科技巨头","tags":[]},{"term":"lease","head":"v. ~ sth (from sb)，~ sth (out) (to sb) to use or let sb","definition":"use sth, especially property or equipment, in exchange for","gloss":"","example":"rentoraregularpayment租用，租借，出租（尤指房地产或设","exampleZh":"备）【️【️考研大纲词汇】 They lease the land from a local farmer.他们从当地一位农场 主手中租得这块土地。 美国超大规模云厂商似乎同样热情不减。9月，亚马逊云服 务表示，正在扩大与HUMAIN的合作，以期在2028年前提供 更多数据中心容量。上月，微软表示将于11月启用更多区域容 量；该公司已从AlMoammar租用沙特站点，并正与阿联酋电 信企业Du合作，在阿联酋建设数据中心。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"tariff","head":"n. /ˈtærɪf/ a list of fixed prices that are charged by a","definition":"hotel or restaurant for rooms, meals, etc., or by a company","gloss":"","example":"foraparticularservice（旅馆、饭店或服务公司的）价目表，收","exampleZh":"费表【️【️考研大纲词汇】","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"well","head":"adv. to a great extent or degree 很；相当；大大地；远","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"远地【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"awell-lovedtale深受喜爱的故事 The castle is well worth a visit. 这座城堡很值得参观。 尽管战争冲突持续，该地区仍具吸引力，原因有几点。其一 是能源价格低廉：普华永道报告称，海湾地区电价约为每千瓦时 6美分，而美国为9至15美分。大量可再生能源和新输电基础 设施进一步压低了成本。其二是土地价格低廉：据普华永道数据， 沙特数据中心工业用地价格为每平方米10至50美元，远低于 美国北弗吉尼亚州的150至600美元，美国许多服务器集群便 坐落于此。另一家咨询机构麦肯锡估算，在海湾地区建设和供电 一座100兆瓦人工智能数据中心，成本为每兆瓦时200至220 美元，低到几乎与中国相当。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"hub","head":"n. ~ (of sth) the central and most important part of a","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"particularplaceoractivity（某地或活动的）中心，核心","exampleZh":"the commercial hub of the city 城市的商业中心","tags":[]},{"term":"inflow","head":"n. the movement of a lot of money, people or things","definition":"","gloss":"intoaplacefromsomewhereelse（资金、人或事物的）流入，","example":"SYN influx The Swiss wanted to discourage an inflow of foreign","exampleZh":"涌入 money.瑞士人想要阻止外资流入。","tags":[]},{"term":"reverse","head":"v. to change sth completely so that it is the","definition":"","gloss":"oppositeofwhatitwasbefore颠倒；彻底转变；使完全相反","example":"The government has failed to reverse the economic decline.","exampleZh":"【️【️考研大纲词汇】 to reverse a procedure/process/trend 彻底改变程序╱过程╱ 趋势 政府未能扭转经济滑坡的趋势。 海湾地区还确立了其行业人才中心的地位：去年，阿联酋和 沙特阿拉伯的人工智能人才净流入量（相对于其劳动力规模而言） 位于全球前列。而且，目前没有证据表明，战事已使这一人才流 入趋势发生逆转。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"deep pocket phrasea source of substantial wealth (usually","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"plural)深口袋：拥有大量财力的个人或组织；也可指雄厚的财力","exampleZh":"或财源","tags":[]},{"term":"paymaster","head":"n. a person or group of people that pays","definition":"another person or organization and therefore can control","gloss":"","example":"theiractions操纵者；后台老板","exampleZh":"此外，海湾国家财力雄厚。7月，阿联酋国有基金MGX筹 集500亿美元用于投资人工智能。其中大部分资金将流向海外 企业，但希望从中分一杯羹的企业，将急于通过在该地区投资来 让出资方满意。","tags":[]},{"term":"underwrite","head":"v. to accept financial responsibility for an","definition":"activity so that you will pay for special costs or for losses it","gloss":"maymake承担经济责任（包括支付特别费用或损失）","example":"The government will have to create a special agency to","exampleZh":"underwrite small business loans. 政府将不得不建立一个专门 机构来为小额企业贷款提供担保。","tags":[]},{"term":"deploy","head":"v. to move soldiers or weapons into a position","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"where they are ready for military action 部署，调度（军队或","exampleZh":"武器） 2 000 troops were deployed in the area.那个地区部署了 2 000人的部队。","tags":[]},{"term":"sovereignty","head":"n. /ˈsɒvrənti/ ~ (over sth)complete power to","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"governacountry主权；最高统治权；最高权威","exampleZh":"The country claimed sovereignty over the island.那个国家声 称对该岛拥有主权。 the sovereignty of Parliament 议会的最高权威","tags":[]},{"term":"build-out phrase an urban planner ’ s estimate of the","head":"","definition":"amount and location of potential development for an area","gloss":"","example":"增建，扩建","exampleZh":"海湾国家的国内政策将需要更多数据中心，这实际上为需 求提供了担保。4月，阿联酋表示将在半数政府部门部署“代 理式人工智能”。该国《国家云安全政策》要求政府实体和关 键基础设施运营者实现“运营主权”，这进一步支撑了数据中 心扩建；沙特阿拉伯的金融机构则普遍被要求使用境内云服务。 麦肯锡的卢卡·本尼奇（LucaBennici）指出，海湾地区私营企 业对数据保护和主权问题“的担忧在日益加剧”。","tags":[]},{"term":"resent","head":"v. /r ɪ ˈ zent/ to feel bitter or angry about sth,","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"especially because you feel it is unfair 愤恨；感到气愤；愤愤","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"on the/sb’s doorstep phrasevery close to where a person","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"lives在某人的住所旁","example":"The nightlife is great with bars and clubs right on the","exampleZh":"doorstep.有这些酒吧和夜总会位于家门口，夜生活真是棒极了。","tags":[]},{"term":"bash","head":"v. /bæʃ/ to criticize sb/sth strongly 严厉批评","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"Bashing politicians is normal practice in the press. 严厉批","exampleZh":"判政治人物乃是新闻界常事。 更重要的是，西方公众针对数据中心的反对日益显现，许多 人对住所附近的高耗能设施感到不满，但这种情况在海湾地区却 很少见。抨击数据中心已在美国政治成为一种流行的竞选策略。 在海湾地区则不然。该地区一位高管表示，这得益于“集中决 策”。","tags":[]},{"term":"craft","head":"v. to make sth using special skills, especially with your","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"hands（尤指用手工）精心制作【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"All the furniture is crafted from natural materials. 所有的家 具均采用天然材料精心制作而成。 a carefully crafted speech 精心准备的讲话","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"embassy","head":"n. /ˈembəsi/ the building in which an embassy","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"works大使馆（指馆舍）","exampleZh":"a demonstration outside the Russian Embassy 在俄罗斯大使 馆外的示威游行","tags":[]},{"term":"moot","head":"v. /muːt/ to suggest an idea for people to discuss 提","definition":"","gloss":"出…供讨论","example":"SYN propose, put forward","exampleZh":"Plans have been mooted for a 450,000-strong army. 建立 一支拥有45万士兵的大军的计划被提出供讨论。 诚然，战争扰乱了海湾地区精心打造的经济繁荣。但战争也 使该地区的执政者更加坚定地要保障其数字投资的安全。另一家 咨询机构Alvarez&Marsal的小库尔特·戴维斯（KurtDavis junior）指出，计划将数据中心打造得如使馆般安全、甚至将其 设于地下的方案正在酝酿中。尽管如此，数据中心扩建仍在继续。 September 12TH-18TH ｜Business","tags":[]}]}],"tests":[{"file":"【福利】9.18 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","type":"reading","instructions":[],"passage":[],"items":[{"number":21,"stem":"The author mentions Iranian drones and Stargate UAE in Paragraph 1 in order to _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"show that war has attacked data-centre projects but has not stopped their construction"},{"key":"B","text":"prove that Gulf governments have abandoned digital infrastructure for military spending"},{"key":"C","text":"suggest that Abu Dhabi's data centre was completed before the war began"},{"key":"D","text":"explain why American cloud firms refuse to invest in the Gulf during conflicts"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"[A]","analysis":["【题型】例证题·开篇案例功能","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1","【解析】","- 原文（Para.1）：Soon after war broke out in the Gulf, Iranian drones targeted Amazon’s data centres in the United Arab Emirates (UAE) and Bahrain.","- 原文（Para.1）：But at Stargate UAE, a 1-gigawatt data centre being built on a 5GW campus in Abu Dhabi, work “never stopped,” says an executive at a state-backed artificial-intelligence firm.","分析：","- 选项A（正确）：无人机攻击说明战争确实威胁数据中心；work never stopped 与首期工程接近完工形成对照，引出战争未阻止建设的主题。","- 选项B（错误）：反向事实陷阱。原文说 boom 未停止，不是放弃数字基础设施。","- 选项C（错误）：时态偷换陷阱。Stargate UAE is being built，首期 almost complete，并非战前已完成。","- 选项D（错误）：反向细节陷阱。后文说美国 hyperscalers 仍有投资热情。","【命题技巧】","- 战争与工程对照：targeted 与 never stopped 形成主题张力。","- 开篇例子关联标题：案例服务于全文核心：战争未遏制海湾数据中心热潮。"]},{"number":22,"stem":"According to Paragraphs 4 to 7, which of the following is true about the Gulf's data-centre boom?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Electricity in the Gulf is more expensive than the average tariff in America"},{"key":"B","text":"Industrial land in Saudi Arabia costs more than comparable land in northern Virginia"},{"key":"C","text":"Cheap energy and land, together with state money and domestic policies, support the build-out"},{"key":"D","text":"The war has clearly reversed the region's net inflow of AI workers"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"[C]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·多因素正误判断","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 4-7","【解析】","- 原文（Para.4）：One is cheap energy: electricity tariffs in the Gulf are around six cents per kilowatt hour, compared with between nine and 15 cents in America...","- 原文（Para.4）：Another is cheap land: according to PwC, industrial land for data centres in Saudi Arabia costs $10-50 per square metre, well below the $150-600 in northern Virginia...","- 原文（Para.6）：In July MGX, an Emirati state-run fund, raised $50bn to invest in AI.","- 原文（Para.7）：Domestic policies in the Gulf will require more data centres, in effect underwriting demand.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：数字反向陷阱。海湾电价约 six cents，低于美国 nine to 15 cents。","- 选项B（错误）：数字反向陷阱。沙特工业用地价格远低于北弗吉尼亚。","- 选项C（正确）：第 4 段列出低电价和低地价，第 6 段说明国家资本雄厚，第 7 段说明国内政策创造需求，共同支撑建设潮。","- 选项D（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。原文说 no evidence that war has sent this flow of talent into reverse。","【命题技巧】","- 多因素归纳：成本、资本、人才与政策需要合并理解。","- 数字方向核对：比较结构中的低于/高于是本题关键。"]},{"number":23,"stem":"The phrase “deep pockets” (Paragraph 6) most probably refers to Gulf states' _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"hidden borrowing from overseas commercial banks"},{"key":"B","text":"strict limits on foreign technology investment"},{"key":"C","text":"control over national cloud-security regulations"},{"key":"D","text":"abundant financial resources available for investment"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"[D]","analysis":["【题型】词义猜测题·习语语境理解","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 6","【解析】","- 原文（Para.6）：Then there are the Gulf states’ deep pockets. In July MGX, an Emirati state-run fund, raised $50bn to invest in AI.","- 原文（Para.6）：Most of that money will flow to overseas companies, but those wanting a slice of it will be eager to keep their paymasters happy by investing in the region.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：无中生有陷阱。原文说 state-run fund raised $50bn，不是海外商业银行秘密借款。","- 选项B（错误）：概念偷换陷阱。第 7 段的监管政策与 deep pockets 的财政含义不同。","- 选项C（错误）：段落错位陷阱。cloud-security regulations 是后文支撑需求的因素，不是该短语含义。","- 选项D（正确）：下文用 $50bn、money、paymasters 解释该习语，指可用于投资的雄厚资金。","【命题技巧】","- 习语下义线索：具体金额和 paymasters 直接解释 deep pockets。","- 相邻段落概念分离：资金优势与监管优势不能混淆。"]},{"number":24,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraphs 7 and 8 that the Gulf's political and policy environment makes data centres _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"dependent on continuous approval from local residents and their community campaign groups"},{"key":"B","text":"easier to build than in parts of the West where public resistance has grown"},{"key":"C","text":"legally exempt from every security requirement imposed by national government regulators"},{"key":"D","text":"less attractive to foreign firms that must store their data inside the country"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】推理判断题·环境对比推理","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 7-8","【解析】","- 原文（Para.7）：The country’s National Cloud Security Policy requires “operational sovereignty” for government entities and operators of critical infrastructure, further supporting the build-out...","- 原文（Para.8）：What is more, there is little of the public opposition to data centres increasingly on show in the West, where many people resent power-hungry facilities on their doorstep... “Centralised decision making” helps, says an executive in the region.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反向环境陷阱。海湾 little public opposition，而西方才面临日益明显的公众抵制。","- 选项B（正确）：国内政策要求本地化和主权运营，创造需求；公众反对少且决策集中，可推知建设环境比部分西方地区更顺畅。","- 选项C（错误）：绝对化陷阱。政策不是免除安全要求，而是提出 operational sovereignty 等要求并因此推动建设。","- 选项D（错误）：反向推理陷阱。本地数据要求吸引或促使投资落地，不是降低吸引力。","【命题技巧】","- 区域对比推理：Gulf 与 West 的公众态度和决策机制形成对照。","- 政策需求识别：underwriting demand 表明监管要求反而支撑建设。"]},{"number":25,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Cheap Energy Alone: Why Gulf Data Centres Need No Policy Support"},{"key":"B","text":"Silicon Dunes: War Has Not Stopped the Gulf's Data-Centre Boom"},{"key":"C","text":"High-Security Architecture: How Underground Bunkers Became a Gulf Policy Obsession"},{"key":"D","text":"Western Backlash: The End of Global Data-Centre Investment Everywhere"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】主旨大意题·最佳标题","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Full text","【解析】","- 原文（Para.2）：Last year PwC, a consultancy, predicted that across the Gulf data-centre capacity would rise fourfold within five years, to about 4GW. The outbreak of war has not halted the boom.","- 原文（Para.4）：Several factors explain the region’s continued attraction, despite the conflict.","- 原文（Para.9）：True, the war has disrupted the Gulf’s carefully crafted economic boom... Nevertheless, the build-out continues.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：以偏概全陷阱。低成本是原因之一，但人才、资本、政策和低反对声音同样重要。","- 选项B（正确）：标题同时概括海湾地区、战争冲击和数据中心建设继续推进的全文主线；Silicon Dunes 保留原文意象。","- 选项C（错误）：细节扩大陷阱。地下化和使馆级安全只是战后在研的安全方案。","- 选项D（错误）：反向主旨陷阱。西方有反对声音，但全文重点是海湾投资继续增长。","【命题技巧】","- 背景-优势-风险结构：战争背景、成本与政策优势、最后安全风险构成文章骨架。","- 标题双要素控制：正确标题需同时包含 war 与 continued boom。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语阅读理解大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。","如果对答案解析有疑惑，直接打开任何AI大模型（如Deepseek、Kimi等），上传该篇原文文档，然后复制粘贴对应的题目和选项，说清楚你的疑问，大模型会回应解释对应的问题。"]}]},{"file":"【福利】9.18检验题__完型填空(1).docx","type":"cloze","instructions":["Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)"],"passage":["The war has not diminished the Gulf’s advantages. Several factors explain the region’s continued ____【11】____, despite the conflict. One is cheap energy: electricity ____【12】____ in the Gulf are around six cents per kilowatt hour, compared with between nine and 15 cents in America, reports PwC. Vast amounts of renewable power and new transmission infrastructure have ____【13】____ costs lower. Another is cheap land: according to PwC, industrial land for data centres in Saudi Arabia costs $10-50 per square metre, well below the $150-600 in northern Virginia, where many of America’s server farms ____【14】____.","The Gulf has also established itself as a ____【15】____ for industry talent: last year the UAE and Saudi Arabia were among the countries that recorded the highest net ____【16】____ of AI workers relative to their workforces. There is no evidence that war has sent this flow of talent into ____【17】____.","Then there are the Gulf states’ deep ____【18】____. In July MGX, an Emirati state-run fund, raised $50bn to invest in AI. Most of that money will flow to overseas companies, but those wanting a ____【19】____ of it will be eager to keep their paymasters happy by ____【20】____ in the region."],"items":[{"number":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"isolation"},{"key":"B","text":"attraction"},{"key":"C","text":"resistance"},{"key":"D","text":"uncertainty"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (attraction)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·因果语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第1句","【解析】","[A] isolation（孤立）：与投资继续涌入相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] attraction（吸引力）：continued attraction 指该地区持续吸引投资。正确答案。","[C] resistance（阻力）：与 several factors explain boom 的语境不合。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] uncertainty（不确定性）：不是优势来源。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"budgets"},{"key":"B","text":"subsidies"},{"key":"C","text":"tariffs"},{"key":"D","text":"profits"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (tariffs)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·能源价格","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] budgets（预算）：不是预算数值。语义场干扰。","[B] subsidies（补贴）：低电价可能与补贴相关，但文意是电价收费标准。近义干扰。","[C] tariffs（收费标准）：electricity tariffs 指电费费率。正确答案。","[D] profits（利润）：不是电力公司利润。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"pushed"},{"key":"B","text":"kept"},{"key":"C","text":"left"},{"key":"D","text":"forced"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (pushed)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·结果关系","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第3句","【解析】","[A] pushed（推动）：have pushed costs lower 指使成本进一步降低。正确答案。","[B] kept（保持）：只能表示维持，不能体现“更低”的变化。程度差异干扰。","[C] left（留下）：leave... lower 语义不合。搭配干扰。","[D] forced（迫使）：force costs lower 语气过强。程度差异干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"live"},{"key":"B","text":"work"},{"key":"C","text":"compete"},{"key":"D","text":"gather"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (gather)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·地点指代","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第5句","【解析】","[A] live（居住）：server farms live 可拟人化，但下文 farms 的比喻重点不是生存。近义干扰。","[B] work（工作）：不自然。搭配干扰。","[C] compete（竞争）：不是与北弗吉尼亚比较竞争地位。语义场干扰。","[D] gather（聚集、坐落）：where many of America’s server farms gather 指许多服务器农场聚集。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"border"},{"key":"B","text":"hub"},{"key":"C","text":"market"},{"key":"D","text":"target"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (hub)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·中心语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第1句","【解析】","[A] border（边界）：语义不合。语义场干扰。","[B] hub（中心）：a hub for industry talent 指产业人才中心。正确答案。","[C] market（市场）：后文强调人才净流入，不是交易市场。语义场干扰。","[D] target（目标）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"outflow"},{"key":"B","text":"turnover"},{"key":"C","text":"inflow"},{"key":"D","text":"shortage"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (inflow)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·流向语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] outflow（流出）：与 highest 和吸引人才矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] turnover（流动率）：只表示更替，不体现净吸引。语义场干扰。","[C] inflow（流入）：net inflow of AI workers 指AI工作者净流入。正确答案。","[D] shortage（短缺）：与净流入事实相反。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"reverse"},{"key":"B","text":"overdrive"},{"key":"C","text":"balance"},{"key":"D","text":"decline"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (reverse)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·固定搭配","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第3句","【解析】","[A] reverse（逆转）：send... into reverse 指使人才流向逆转。正确答案。","[B] overdrive（过度运转）：不表示方向改变。语义场干扰。","[C] balance（平衡）：不能接 sent into 的方向含义。搭配干扰。","[D] decline（下降）：语义接近，但没有 send into decline 与 flow of talent 的方向搭配自然。近义干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"concerns"},{"key":"B","text":"debts"},{"key":"C","text":"rivals"},{"key":"D","text":"pockets"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (pockets)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·财富语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第1句","【解析】","[A] concerns（担忧）：与后文巨额募资矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] debts（债务）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] rivals（对手）：不是竞争者。语义场干扰。","[D] pockets（财力）：deep pockets 为固定表达，指资金雄厚。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"record"},{"key":"B","text":"slice"},{"key":"C","text":"sense"},{"key":"D","text":"monopoly"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (slice)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·份额搭配","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第3句","【解析】","[A] record（记录）：语义无关。语义场干扰。","[B] slice（一份）：a slice of it 指获得其中一部分资金。正确答案。","[C] sense（感觉）：不与 wanting a... of it 构成份额义。搭配干扰。","[D] monopoly（垄断）： overseas companies 竞争份额，不是垄断。程度差异干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"travelling"},{"key":"B","text":"lobbying"},{"key":"C","text":"investing"},{"key":"D","text":"training"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (investing)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·动词语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第3句","【解析】","[A] travelling（旅行）：与商业回报无关。语义场干扰。","[B] lobbying（游说）：不是通过游说取悦出资方。语义场干扰。","[C] investing（投资）：by investing in the region 指通过在地区投资来取悦出资方。正确答案。","[D] training（培训）：未涉及培训出资方。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语完型填空大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。"]}]},{"file":"【福利】9.18检验题__新题型__小标题匹配(1).docx","type":"heading","instructions":["Directions:"],"passage":["Part B","Read the following text and answer the questions by choosing the most suitable subheading from the list A-G for each of the numbered paragraphs (41-45). There are two extra subheadings. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)","The following paragraphs explain why data-centre construction in the Gulf has continued despite war.","Paragraph 41 Several factors explain the region’s continued attraction, despite the conflict. One is cheap energy: electricity tariffs in the Gulf are around six cents per kilowatt hour, compared with between nine and 15 cents in America, reports PwC. Vast amounts of renewable power and new transmission infrastructure have pushed costs lower. Another is cheap land: according to PwC, industrial land for data centres in Saudi Arabia costs $10-50 per square metre, well below the $150-600 in northern Virginia, where many of America’s server farms live. McKinsey, another consultancy, puts the cost of building and powering a 100-megawatt AI data centre in the Gulf at $200-220 per MW hour, nearly as low as in China.","Paragraph 42 The Gulf has also established itself as a hub for industry talent: last year the UAE and Saudi Arabia were among the countries that recorded the highest net inflow of AI workers relative to their workforces. There is no evidence that war has sent this flow of talent into reverse.","Paragraph 43 Then there are the Gulf states’ deep pockets. In July MGX, an Emirati state-run fund, raised $50bn to invest in AI. Most of that money will flow to overseas companies, but those wanting a slice of it will be eager to keep their paymasters happy by investing in the region.","Paragraph 44 Domestic policies in the Gulf will require more data centres, in effect underwriting demand. In April the UAE said it would deploy “agentic AI” across half of the government. The country’s National Cloud Security Policy requires “operational sovereignty” for government entities and operators of critical infrastructure, further supporting the build-out, while Saudi Arabia’s financial institutions are generally required to use cloud services within the country. Luca Bennici of McKinsey notes that private firms in the Gulf have “growing concerns” of their own about data protection and sovereignty.","Paragraph 45 What is more, there is little of the public opposition to data centres increasingly on show in the West, where many people resent power-hungry facilities on their doorstep. Bashing data centres has turned into a popular campaign strategy in American politics. In the Gulf, not so much. “Centralised decision making” helps, says an executive in the region.","[A] Government policies reinforce demand","[B] State-backed capital deepens commitment","[C] Cost advantages still favour the Gulf","[D] The talent pipeline has not reversed","[E] Public resistance remains limited","[F] War has stopped all new construction","[G] Companies reject local data controls"],"items":[{"number":41,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"C","kicker":"【答案】C","analysis":["【定位】Paragraph 41。","【解析】该段以“Several factors”开启原因分析，先用电力价格对比说明 cheap energy，再用土地价格和 100 兆瓦数据中心的成本说明 cheap land 与建设运营优势。【C】中的 cost advantages 正是对这些价格证据的概括，favour the Gulf 也回应段首 continued attraction。","逐项分析"]},{"number":42,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"D","kicker":"【答案】D","analysis":["【定位】Paragraph 42。","【解析】段首“established itself as a hub for industry talent”提出中心；随后用 UAE 和沙特 AI 工人净流入领先证明，末句“no evidence that war has sent this flow... into reverse”进一步强调方向。【D】的 pipeline has not reversed 是该句的同义概括。","逐项分析"]},{"number":43,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"B","kicker":"【答案】B","analysis":["【定位】Paragraph 43。","【解析】“deep pockets”引出 MGX 这一 Emirati state-run fund，并举出 500 亿美元 AI 投资基金；后文说想获得资金的公司会愿意通过在区域内投资来“keep their paymasters happy”。【B】抓住 state-backed capital 与 commitment 的关系，概括资本对建设热潮的支撑。","逐项分析"]},{"number":44,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"A","kicker":"【答案】A","analysis":["【定位】Paragraph 44。","【解析】段首“Domestic policies... will require more data centres, in effect underwriting demand”就是主题句。随后 UAE 的政府 AI 部署、“operational sovereignty”要求和金融机构本地用云规则，都说明政策直接扩大本地数据中心需求。【A】比单纯说 security 更完整。","逐项分析"]},{"number":45,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"E","kicker":"【答案】E","analysis":["【定位】Paragraph 45。","【解析】段首用“little of the public opposition”确立中心，再以西方居民反感和美国竞选策略作对照；末句借高管之口指出“centralised decision making”有帮助。【E】同时保留 resistance 和 limited 的限定，比“没有反对”更准确。","逐项分析","干扰项设置","【F】利用战争语境把“没有停止”夸大为“全部停止”；【G】利用 data protection 和 sovereignty 复现原词，却把“要求本地主权管控”反写成“企业拒绝管控”。两者都需要用段落方向和限定词排除。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语新题型大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。目前是在测试阶段，该题型仅提供到12月底。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。"]}]}],"qa":[],"originals":[{"kind":"reading","label":"精读","file":"9.18 精读(1).pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":628445,"date":"2026-09-18","range":"","title":"Silicon dunes","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\9.18 精读(1).pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】9.18 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":55474,"date":"2026-09-18","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】9.18 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】9.18检验题__完型填空(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":58265,"date":"2026-09-18","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】9.18检验题__完型填空(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】9.18检验题__新题型__小标题匹配(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":68932,"date":"2026-09-18","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】9.18检验题__新题型__小标题匹配(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"layout","label":"杂志排版","file":"9.18杂志排版(1).pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":726100,"date":"2026-09-18","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\9.18杂志排版(1).pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"}]};
